:false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.6.dev.custom_build [6fd949a6d]\n- Reproducible in v4.5.2.rc.custom_build [6d411f0c0]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev (41ca01d12) - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 19 Sep 2025 16:09:36 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7900 XT (RADV NAVI31) - AMD Ryzen 9 7900X 12-Core Processor (24 threads) - 30.49 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen trying to call the `popup()` method on a Popup as a child of a scene docked in the editor, the following errors appear:\n```\n  ERROR: platform/linuxbsd/wayland/display_server_wayland.cpp:767 - Condition \"root_id == INVALID_WINDOW_ID\" is true.\n  ERROR: A swap chain was not created for the screen.\n  ERROR: A swap chain was not created for the screen.\n  ERROR: A swap chain was not created for the screen.\n  [...]\n  ERROR: platform/linuxbsd/wayland/display_server_wayland.cpp:863 - Condition \"!windows.has(wd.root_id)\" is true.\n```\nThe popup itself never appears, and the swap chain error seems to be spammed once per frame until focusing another window (e.g. Alt+Tab).\n\nThe issue does not occur with the X11 version of the editor.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* Create a plugin, add a scene as a dock.\n* Add a button to the docked scene that loads a popup scene.\n* Click the button.\n\nI will note that this only occurs when preloading the popup scene, not when creating one from scratch with `Popup.new()` (see commented code in MRP).\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[wayland-editor-popup.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23440479/wayland-editor-popup.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions"